rados es 61,7, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 19,5 a 312,6. El contrato [1], de 14.550 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: la acumulación de importes junto al límite es un indicador estadístico. No prueba que se haya partido ningún contrato ni que alguien haya actuado mal; puede deberse a precios de mercado, a presupuestos cerrados o a necesidades distintas.\nQué se puede revisar: en los expedientes enlazados, qué se contrató en cada caso y en qué fechas, y si varios contratos atienden una misma necesidad que pudo contratarse de una vez.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 37 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 0.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 61.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 19.5 to 312.6. December accounts for 0% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 25 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,550 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not mean that any of them were improperly awarded. It could reflect normal market pricing or budget constraints. The data alone does not indicate wrongdoing or improper behavior by any party involved.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what services were provided and the reasons for the specific amount. Also, review the distribution of contracts across different awardees to identify any patterns or potential overlaps in service provision. Look for any repeated orders from the same awardee that might suggest a need for further scrutiny.","origen_es":"plantilla","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["z3U1dsmc76LpxJFXpLZ%2B2A%3D